==Old Norse==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|non|hór|hœgr}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*hauhaz||high}}, from {{der|non|ine-pro|*kewk-||to bend, curve, arch, vault}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|hēah}}, {{cog|ofs|hāch}}, {{cog|osx|hōh}}, {{cog|goh|hōh}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌿𐌷𐍃|tr=[[hauhs#Gothic|hauhs]]|sc=Goth}}.

====Adjective====
{{non-adj|hærri|hæstr}}

# [[high]], [[tall]]

=====Declension=====
{{non-decl-adj|há|há|háv|háv|hárr|nsm=hár|nsn=hátt|comp=hærr|sup=hæst}}

=====Descendants=====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|hár}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|háur}}
* Old Swedish: {{l|gmq-osw|høgher|hø̄gher}}
** Middle Norwegian: {{l|gmq-mno|høg}} (from ca. 1400)
*** Norwegian Nynorsk: {{l|nn|høg}}
**** Norwegian Bokmål: {{l|nb|høg}}
** Swedish: {{l|sv|hög}}
* Danish: {{l|da|høj}}
** Faroese: {{l|fo|høgur}}
** Norwegian Bokmål: {{l|nb|høy}}
